      "math_academy_id": "e-2567",
      "problem": "Given the diagram shown below, what is the value of $x?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14182164/assets/3fe1e3d1e6f89af1050d0437379a811eabb19212be36f0fecd91ddfaca2594ee.png)",
      "worked_solution": "By the segment addition postulate, we have\n\n$$\nAD = AB + BC +CD.\n$$\n\nTo solve for $x,$ we can substitute the given information\n\n$$\nAD=30, \\quad AB=x+5, \\quad BC=13, \\quad CD=5x,\n$$\n\n \n\nand then solve the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =AB+BC+CD \\\\ 30 & =(x+5)+13+5x \\\\ 30 & =6x+18 \\\\ 6x & =12 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
